      "problem": "Given that $X∼U\\{2,3,4,…,13\\},$ compute $P(X=6).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{2,3,4,…,13\\},$ and the set $S=\\{2,3,4,…,13\\}$ has $|S|=13-2+1=12$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12}, & x=2,3,4,…,13 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=6)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{12}.\n$$",
